<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 6 October, from 105 BCE to 1981.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/cimbri" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cimbri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">105 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Cimbri and Teutons crush two Roman armies at Arausio</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-vaucluse">Arausio</a>, now Orange, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbri">Cimbri</a> under Boiorix and the Teutons under Teutobod defeated two Roman armies under the proconsul Quintus Servilius Caepio and the consul Gnaeus Mallius Maximus. It was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s worst defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbrian-war">Cimbrian War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbrian-war">Cimbrian War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">69 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,094 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lucullus defeats Tigranes the Great at Tigranocerta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-mithridatic-war">Third Mithridatic War</a>, a Roman army under the consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-licinius-lucullus">Lucius Licinius Lucullus</a> defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigranes-the-great">Tigranes the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and captured his capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigranocerta">Tigranocerta</a>. The war ended with Armenia an allied client state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-mithridatic-war">Third Mithridatic War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/23">23 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,003 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rebels kill Wang Mang as Chang'an falls</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebel forces broke into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-mang">Wang Mang</a>, the usurper who had founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xin-dynasty">Xin dynasty</a>. His death cleared the way for the restoration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-guangwu-of-han">Emperor Guangwu</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/618">618 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,408 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wang Shichong defeats Li Mi at the Battle of Yanshi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Blockaded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> for months, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-shichong">Wang Shichong</a> led his troops out and surprised Li Mi's besieging army north of Yanshi, winning a decisive victory. Li's followers joined Wang, who later deposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> puppet ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-tong">Yang Tong</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transition-from-sui-to-tang">Transition from Sui to Tang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-mi-sui-dynasty">Li Mi</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1600">1600 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">426 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peri's Euridice, the oldest surviving opera, is performed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacopo-peri">Jacopo Peri</a>'s Euridice was staged at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pitti-palace">Pitti Palace</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> during celebrations for the marriage of Maria de' Medici to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV of France</a>. It is the earliest opera whose music survives complete.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1927">1927 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">99 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Jazz Singer premieres in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Warner Bros released The Jazz Singer, starring Al Jolson, the first feature film with synchronised dialogue and singing. Its success ended the silent era within a few years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Egypt and Syria attack Israel on Yom Kippur</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Egyptian and Syrian forces launched surprise attacks on Israeli positions in Sinai and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a> on the holiest day of the Jewish year. The war ended in Israeli counter-offensives and reshaped Middle Eastern diplomacy.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1981">1981 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">45 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Egyptian president Anwar Sadat is assassinated</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Islamist army officers shot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat">Anwar Sadat</a> during a military parade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> marking the 1973 war. Sadat had signed a peace treaty with Israel in 1979 and shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> with Menachem Begin.</p></div></li></ol>
